#: ../../.opencode/commands/handoff.md:4
msgid ""
"The host-tool Stop hook normally keeps the machine half of NEXT.md fresh "
"on every turn. Use this command when you want to force a full refresh — "
"typically before switching tools, when context feels close to full, or "
"when stepping away."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/handoff.md:9
msgid "**Steps:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/handoff.md:11
msgid ""
"Run `hero next checkpoint` to refresh the machine half right now (branch,"
" recent commits, dirty files, hot files)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/handoff.md:13
msgid "Then rewrite the agent half of NEXT.md if anything in it is stale:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/handoff.md:14
msgid "**Last user ask** — quote the user's most recent meaningful turn"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/handoff.md:15
msgid ""
"**Just finished** — what shipped (only the interesting parts; the machine"
" half lists commits)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/handoff.md:17
msgid "**Next** — the concrete next step + a runnable `→` pointer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/handoff.md:18
msgid "**Blocked on** — actual errors, if any"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/handoff.md:19
msgid "**Tried and failed** — rejected approaches, if any"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/handoff.md:20
msgid ""
"**Context to carry forward** — non-obvious things the next session needs "
"that aren't in `git log` or the spec corpus"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/handoff.md:23
msgid ""
"Run `hero queue write -q` to refresh `.hero/QUEUE.md` so the ranked queue"
" snapshot is current for the next session — important for harnesses "
"(Claude Code) that can't pop a terminal at session start."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/handoff.md:27
msgid ""
"Confirm to the user that NEXT.md and QUEUE.md are current and ready for "
"handoff."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/handoff.md:30
msgid ""
"See `skills/next-md.md` for the NEXT.md format and `skills/kickoff-"
"prompt.md` for the `## Kickoff` sections that populate `hero queue` / "
"QUEUE.md."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/handoff.md:34
msgid ""
"**What to say:** \"handoff\", \"save checkpoint\", \"save session\", "
"\"save state\"."
msgstr ""

